## 2. Typography

**Two font stacks, both system fonts. Zero web fonts.**

| Token | Stack | Usage |
|---|---|---|
| `--font` | `-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif` | Everything |
| `--mono` | `ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, "SF Mono", Menlo, Consolas, monospace` | `.card__id`, `.step__order`, `.phase__index`, `.md-code`, `.md-pre`, `.score-preview b`, `.palette__name`, `.ui-code`, `.wizard-move__index` |

**No Google Fonts, no fontsource, no `@font-face`, no `@import url`, no font files.** Verified: `git grep -in "fonts.googleapis|fontsource|@font-face|@import url" origin/main --` → zero hits; no `.woff2`/`.ttf`/`.otf` files in the tree.

**One font-stack bug:** `.palette__name` uses `var(--font-mono, …)` — `--font-mono` is never defined (the real token is `--mono`), so it silently falls back to the second value in the `var()` fallback chain.

**Type scale:** a *dense, small, rem-based* scale. The design is typographically quiet — the largest text on screen is the hero line at `clamp(1.55rem, 3.4vw, 2.25rem)`. Body copy is `0.88–0.92rem`. Micro-labels are `0.62–0.72rem`, uppercase, weight 600, tracked `0.06em–0.16em`. Headings use negative tracking (`-0.01em` to `-0.035em`). Numeric data uses `font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums` (meters, stats, rail counts, card formulas, jobmap indices). See the full type scale table in §1d.

