<div class="studio-app">                    ← 100dvh, flex column, overflow hidden
  <main class="stage">                      ← flex 1, radial indigo glows
    <StudioBar />                           ← 56px, the ONLY persistent chrome
    <div class="stage__split">              ← flex row
      <div class="stage__thread">           ← flex 1, min-width 0
        <WorkbenchRail />                   ← artifact chips, ABOVE the thread
        <ChatStage />                       ← hero/welcome OR transcript + composer dock
      </div>
      <WorkspacePanel />                    ← the LENS, docks RIGHT of the thread
    </div>
  </main>
  <ChangelogModal />                        ← overlay, z 2000
  <Toasts />                                ← bottom-right stack, z 1000
</div>
```

### The three-zone anatomy

**1. The Bar (56px, `.bar`)** — left: `brand brand--home` (mark + "Living Studio" wordmark, clicking = go home). Right: "✨ What's New" changelog pill, `+` new conversation icon-button, bell icon-button (with `.bell-badge` count), health pill (`.status-dot` + "Live"/"Local mode"/"Connecting"), settings icon-button. **No navigation lives in the bar** — the artifacts carry navigation.

**2. The Rail (`.rail`)** — horizontally-scrolling chip strip, centered on the same 720px column as the thread. It is **data-derived, not a menu**: it renders `null` until the thread has produced something.

| Chip | Appears when | Opens |
|---|---|---|
| `Landscape · N` | `canvas.outcomes.length > 0` | `landscape` panel |
| `Job map · N` | `canvas.steps.length > 0` | `jobmap` panel |
| `Evidence · N` | outcomes with non-empty `evidence` | `evidence` panel |

Chips are `5px 9px` padded, 8px radius, transparent border, `--faint` → `--text` on hover, with a tabular-nums count.

**3. The Thread (`.chat`)** — two states:
- **Empty**: `.chat__welcome` centers a 720px column (`margin-block: auto`) containing `Hero` (eyebrow / big greeting / sub / suggestion pills) with the `Composer` directly beneath it. Bottom padding `max(56px, 14vh)` lifts it off the edge on tall screens.
- **Active**: `.chat__scroll` (scrollable transcript, `role="log" aria-live="polite"`) + `.chat__dock` (sticky composer, `linear-gradient(to top, var(--bg) 60%, transparent)`).

**Column widths:** thread `max-width: 720px`, `margin: 0 auto`. Composer max 220px tall, grows with the draft, `border-radius: 22px` pill shape, `rgba(255,255,255,0.035)` fill.

### The "lens" concept — YES, it's central

`WorkspacePanel.tsx` docstring: *"A lens on the conversation, not a place you go."*

- **≥1024px**: docks as a **right-hand column**, `width: min(520px, 44vw)`, `min-width: 360px`, `border-left: 1px solid var(--line)`, background `linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(255,255,255,0.022), rgba(255,255,255,0.006))` over `var(--bg-raised)`. It is **not modal** — `role="complementary"`, no scrim, the composer stays live and focused to its left.
- **<1024px**: becomes a fixed full-screen overlay (`position: fixed; inset: 0; z-index: 60`) with a `.scrim` (`rgba(0,0,0,0.55)` + `backdrop-filter: blur(2px)`) and `role="dialog" aria-modal="true"`.
- **Anatomy**: `.lens__head` (icon tile 30×30 / title / one-line blurb / close button) → `.lens__body` (scrollable, `scrollbar-gutter: stable`) → `.lens__foot` (the point of the design: a note *"A lens on the conversation, not a separate place."* + a full-width button that **closes the lens and sends a panel-specific question back to the thread**).

**The five lenses** (`workspace/panels.tsx`): `catchup`, `landscape`, `jobmap`, `evidence`, `capture` — plus a separate `settings` panel (opened from the bar, not the rail).

**Design intent, from `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-21-conversation-first-studio-design.md`:** *"The conversation owns the stage at every moment."* The old 264px drawer was **deleted**, not shrunk.

