## 7. The inline surfaces catalog

**Path:** `apps/studio/src/ui/catalog.ts` — *"The closed catalog of surfaces the agent may compose."*

Two tiers: **9 primitives** (composition) + **6 cards** (named ODI shapes) = **15 surfaces**. The file is the single source of truth: `catalogManifest()` travels to the sidecar; `catalogPrompt()` is what the model reads.

**Shared `actions` prop** (auto-added to every entry unless `actions: false`): array of `{ label: string, intent: string, tone?: "primary" | "ghost" }`. `label` = "Short imperative label, two to four words." `intent` = "The full message to send when clicked, written as the user would say it." `tone`: "Use primary at most once per surface." Clicks dispatch the intent back to the agent as the user's next message.

### Tier 1 — Primitives (9)

| Type | kind | Description (verbatim) | Fields rendered | Required |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `stack` | layout | "Vertical or horizontal grouping. The default container for anything that is not a card." | `direction: "vertical"\|"horizontal"` (default vertical), `gap: "sm"\|"md"\|"lg"` (default md), `actions`; **accepts children** | — |
| `grid` | layout | "Two or three equal columns for parallel ideas — options, before/after, comparable outcomes." | `columns: integer 2–3`, `gap: "sm"\|"md"\|"lg"`; **accepts children**; no actions | `columns` |
| `heading` | leaf | "A section heading. Use sparingly — at most one per reply." | `text: string`, `level: integer 2–3` (2 = section → `<h3>`, 3 = sub → `<h4>`) | `text` |
| `text` | leaf | "A block of prose. Keep it to one or two sentences; cards carry the evidence." | `text: string` (supports inline `**bold**`, `*italic*`, `` `code` ``), `tone: "default"\|"muted"\|"positive"\|"warning"\|"critical"` | `text` |
| `list` | leaf | "A short bulleted or numbered list. Use for steps and enumerations, not for evidence." | `items: string[]` (1–10), `marker: "dot"\|"number"\|"check"` (`dot`→`<ul>`, `number`→`<ol>`) | `items` |
| `stat` | leaf | "A single headline number with its label and an optional delta." | `label: string`, `value: string` (pre-formatted, e.g. "-90%" or "8.9 / 10"), `delta: string`, `tone: "neutral"\|"positive"\|"warning"\|"critical"` | `label`, `value` |
| `meter` | leaf | "A labelled 0–10 bar. Use to make an importance or satisfaction rating visible." | `label: string`, `value: number 0–10`, `max: number 1–10` (default 10), `tone` | `label`, `value` |
| `callout` | leaf | "A bordered note that demands attention: a risk, a verdict, a piece of guidance." | `tone: "info"\|"positive"\|"warning"\|"critical"`, `title: string`, `body: string` | `tone`, `body` |
| `divider` | leaf | "A thin rule between sections." | *(none)* | — |

### Tier 2 — Cards (6)

| Type | kind | Description (verbatim) | Fields rendered | Required |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `outcome-card` | leaf | "One desired outcome with its ODI scores and opportunity score. Your default answer when discussing a single outcome." | `id: string` (e.g. "O-1"), `statement: string` ("The outcome in strict ODI form: direction + unit + object + context"), `importance: number 0–10`, `satisfaction: number 0–10`, `opportunityScore: number 0–20` ("Omit it — the score is computed from importance and satisfaction"), `evidence: string` ("The customer voice behind the rating"), `actions` | `id`, `statement`, `importance`, `satisfaction` |
| `opportunity-board` | leaf | "A ranked table of outcomes by opportunity score. Use when comparing several needs at once." | `title: string`, `outcomes: array` (1–12) of `{ id, statement, importance, satisfaction, opportunityScore }`; rendered as a 2-column table (Outcome / Opportunity), sorted by score desc | `outcomes` |
| `impact-simulation` | leaf | "A before/after simulation of a proposed bet against one outcome. This is the WYSIWYG of human impact." | `outcome: { id, statement }`, `bet: string` ("The product bet being tested, in plain words"), `before: string[]` (1–6, "Today's reality, concrete and measured"), `after: string[]` (1–6, "The world with the bet shipped, equally concrete"), `metrics: array` (≤4) of `{ label, value, delta }`, `verdict: string` ("One sentence: build it, reshape it, or drop it.") | `outcome`, `bet`, `before`, `after` |
| `evidence-quote` | leaf | "A verbatim customer signal with its source and lineage. Use instead of paraphrasing research." | `source: string` ("Where it came from, e.g. \"Gong call #104 — FinTech Corp\""), `quote: string` ("Exact words. Never paraphrase inside this field."), `linkedTo: string` ("The job or outcome it supports, e.g. \"JOB-402 / O-1\""), `severity: "low"\|"medium"\|"high"\|"critical"` | `source`, `quote` |
| `job-map` | leaf | "The eight universal job stages for one job, in order. Use to show where in the process friction lives." | `job: string`, `steps: array` (1–8) of `{ name: string, stage: "define"\|"locate"\|"prepare"\|"confirm"\|"execute"\|"monitor"\|"modify"\|"conclude", note: string }` | `job`, `steps` |
| `decision-record` | leaf | "A Product Decision Record: the bet, the outcome it serves, and why it was chosen." | `title: string`, `outcomeId: string`, `bet: string`, `rationale: string`, `status: "proposed"\|"approved"\|"rejected"` | `title`, `bet`, `rationale` |

### Domain logic baked into rendering (`apps/studio/src/lib/odi.ts`)

```
opportunityScore = importance + max(importance − satisfaction, 0)
isUnderserved    = score > 10     (threshold constant UNDERSERVED_THRESHOLD = 10)
formatOpportunityScore = score.toFixed(1)  ("N/A" if null)
opportunityPill  = score > 10 → { label: "🔥 Underserved (Opp: N.N)", variant: "amber" }
                   else      → { label: "✓ Served (Opp: N.N)",      variant: "green" }
```

The `outcome-card` renders the formula literally: *"Opportunity = importance + max(importance − satisfaction, 0) = N.N"*.

**Severity → tone:** `low`→neutral, `medium`→info, `high`→warning, `critical`→critical.
**Status → tone:** `proposed`→info, `approved`→positive, `rejected`→critical.

**Protocol limits** (`ui/protocol.ts`): `maxDepth: 12`, `maxNodes: 200`, `maxStringLength: 2000`, `maxChildren: 32`, `maxActions: 40`. Over-limit input is rejected whole.

